# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bottom panel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description One pane, showing the register or the report of the selected tab.
\ An optional panel below it holds everything that is not the
\ register itself -- an import waiting to be accepted, or the
\ results of a find -- each in a tab of its own, so more than one can
\ be open and read at once.
Details The panel is open exactly when it has a tab in it, and closes itself
\ when the last one does: accepting or cancelling an import closes that
\ tab, closing a find's results closes that one, and the panel is gone
\ once nothing is left. Opening a new one -- a second find, an import
\ started from another register -- adds a tab rather than replacing
\ what is already open, and the one just opened becomes active, the
\ same rule a register tab already follows.
\
\ There used to be a Split view on the menu, two registers side by side
\ for reading two accounts at once, and before that an import was shown
\ the same way -- as a second pane beside the register, rather than in
\ this panel. Both are gone. A window that can be left in a two-register
\ state shows two registers on the next launch with nothing to say why;
\ the panel's tabs say why for themselves, and more than one thing can
\ wait to be judged at once, which a single second pane could not do
\ either. Reading two registers at once is worth having again one day as
\ two windows, not as a mode this one can be left in.

Scenario The bottom panel is closed until something opens it
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then bottom panel is : BottomPanel Vertical
| Open      | false |
| TabCount  | 0     |
| ActiveTab | 0     |

Attributes BottomPanel
Description Whether the panel below the register is open, and how many tabs
\ are in it.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Open      | Boolean | false   |
| TabCount  | Integer | 0       |
| ActiveTab | Integer | 0       |

DataType BottomPanelTabKind
Description What one tab of the bottom panel is showing.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value        | Notes                                             |
| ImportReview | An import waiting to be looked over and accepted  |
| FindResults  | The transactions a find matched                   |

Attributes BottomPanelTabRow
Description One tab of the bottom panel, in the order it was opened.
| Attribute | Type               | Default      |
| Tab       | Integer            | 0            |
| Kind      | BottomPanelTabKind | ImportReview |
| Active    | Boolean            | false        |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reviewing an import in the bottom panel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description An import is shown in a tab of the bottom panel rather than in a
\ dialog of its own, so that the register it is about to change stays
\ in view while it is read. Nothing reaches the book until it is
\ accepted.

Attributes ImportReviewRow
Description One row of an import waiting to be reviewed. Account is where the
\ money moved; Category is the other side as the import worked it out.
| Attribute   | Type              | Default    |
| Line        | Integer           | 0          |
| Date        | Date              | 2026-01-01 |
| Payee       | PayeeName         | none       |
| Account     | AccountPath       | none       |
| Category    | AccountPath       | none       |
| Amount      | Money             | 0.00       |
| Disposition | ImportDisposition | New        |
| Accepted    | Boolean           | true       |
| Identifier  | FitId             | none       |
| Source      | ImportSource      | Ofx        |
| RawName     | Text              | none       |
| Memo        | Text              | none       |
| CheckNo     | CheckNumber       | none       |
| Cleared     | ClearedStatus     | Cleared    |

