# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What accepting an import keeps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description An accepted row keeps what the file called it.
\
\ A downloaded row arrives with the name the file gave it -- a FITID
\ from a QFX, whatever the bank's CSV uses for a reference -- and that
\ name is the whole reason a second download of the same statement
\ does nothing. So it has to reach the transaction that is stored.
Details The review shows a row as date, payee, account, category and amount,
\ because that is what a person reads. Building the transaction back out
\ of those five columns would lose the identifier, and the loss would be
\ silent: the import would look right, the register would look right,
\ and next month's download of the same account would offer every
\ transaction in it again as new.
\
\ So what the import prepared is what is stored. The columns on the
\ screen are a view of it, not the source of it.
\
\ The raw name travels the same way and for a related reason: a rule
\ written next year has to be able to match what the bank sent this
\ year, so what the bank sent is kept rather than only what it was
\ turned into. The memo, the check number and whether the bank has
\ settled the row travel with it for no deeper reason than that the file
\ said so and the review is not the place to lose it.
\
\ Whether a row arrives settled is the import's to say, not the review's:
\ an OFX file's rows are a statement and are cleared, and a CSV says
\ nothing about what the bank has settled. So the review carries what it
\ was given rather than deciding.

Attributes AcceptedTransaction
Description A transaction that accepting the review has just added, with the
\ identifier it was imported under. Only the accepted rows are
\ listed; what the book already held is not.
| Attribute     | Type          | Default   |
| SourceAccount | AccountPath   |           |
| Destination   | AccountPath   | none      |
| Amount        | Money         | 0.00      |
| Identifier | FitId         | none      |
| Source     | ImportSource  | Ofx       |
| RawName    | Text          | none      |
| Memo       | Text          | none      |
| CheckNo    | CheckNumber   | none      |
| Cleared    | ClearedStatus | Uncleared |

Scenario Accepting an import keeps the identifier the file gave each row
Description The identifier belongs to the side the statement is for. The bank
\ has never heard of the category, so that side carries none.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
| Line | Date       | Payee         | Account         | Category           | Amount | Disposition | Identifier  | Source | RawName                      | Memo          | CheckNo |
| 1    | 2026-02-02 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking | Expenses:Groceries | -52.10 | New         | 20260202001 | Ofx    | HARRIS~TEETER~#231~DURHAM~NC | Weekly~shop   | none    |
When import accepted
Then accepted transactions are : AcceptedTransaction
| SourceAccount   | Destination        | Amount | Identifier  | Source | RawName                      | Memo        | CheckNo | Cleared |
| Assets:Checking | Expenses:Groceries | -52.10 | 20260202001 | Ofx    | HARRIS~TEETER~#231~DURHAM~NC | Weekly~shop | none    | Cleared |

